cat << EOF
Fcitx5 is a lightweight and flexible input method framework which aims to
be language independent and provides a clean and well designed API.

It supports X11 (via XIM and the XCB input method protocol) as well as
Wayland (via the input-method and virtual-keyboard protocols), and ships
the following engines and user interfaces out of the box:

  * keyboard layout engine
  * classic (X11/Wayland) candidate window UI
  * XIM server and XCB frontend
  * DBus based configuration interface
  * spell checking and emoji support

Input method engines such as Pinyin are provided by
fcitx5-chinese-addons, while toolkit glue lives in fcitx5-qt and
fcitx5-gtk.
EOF
